    "turn_text": "Howdy, this is AI Brian, as real Brian is still stuck in lake effects snow somewhere in the Great White North. Today, we're going to do a special flashback episode of the Brian Nichols show as we're traveling back to 2019 to revisit my conversation with a congressman who has since become one of the most discussed and debated figures in American politics. Thomas Massey, before he became known for his bold stands on spending bills, the speaker race and government insanity, his fierce opposition to foreign aid, and his headline making procedural challenges that have both frustrated leadership and energized his supporters. Congressman Massey sat down with me to share his fascinating journey from inventor to liberty-minded representative. In this candid conversation from five years ago, you'll hear Massey discuss everything from his early days fighting local government over-reaching Kentucky to his initial impressions of then-President Trump and the deep state. What's particularly striking is how many of the issues he raised from government surveillance to the manipulation of congressional rules. continue to dominate our political discourse today. So join me as we look back at this revealing conversation with a man who would go on to become one of Congress's most influential and controversial voices for liberty, Thomas Massey. on the show Congressman Thomas Massey here on the Brian it will show absolutely Congressman you've been very busy today because today over in DC which is otherwise known as the swamp up here in the northeast you guys ended up voting on the continuing resolution which will dig into a little bit more because it was absolutely insane but thankfully we got somebody like you there fighting the good fight so for anybody who is living under a rock Could you maybe do a little quick introduction, Congressman? Really, who are you? And what was your Liberty story to get you to where you are today?",
