    "turn_text": "Oh, okay. I'll try and give you a quick version. I grew up in Kentucky. I was an inventor as a kid. I built robot arms for science fairs. I was kind of geeky. and I wanted to go to MIT, so I ended up going to the Massachusetts Institute of Technology. I got a degree in electrical engineering, degree in mechanical engineering, started a company while I was there, raised venture capital, did that for 10 years, sold my ownership in the company, moved back to Kentucky, and really hadn't been paying much attention to politics, but I started reading the local paper, and I noticed that The local politicians were trying to raise our taxes, zone our property, force people who didn't need a sewer system because they had septic tanks that worked fine, force them to sign up for something they didn't need using imminent domain, like lots of sort of ugly things to liver tarians",
