    "turn_text": "So my show obviously is reaching a lot more, I'd say, you know, the small L or even in many cases, big L libertarians, right? And I think there's been a pretty big split in the larger libertarian circles because a lot of libertarian folks look at Trump as, you know, kind of this guy with a hammer just going through the China shop and just smashing everything in his way, whereas others are looking him as, you know, truly a threat to our liberty. And I think it's been a really hard, I mean, to say it's hard to get libertarians to agree on anything is, you know, an understatement of the year. But to really look and say, you know, as somebody who's in the fray of things, being your self-congressment, what would you say to libertarians to kind of give them a little bit more insight that you're experiencing behind the scenes in terms of Trump's, you know, either his good feelings or his bad feelings towards the concept of liberty?",
