    "turn_text": "Yeah. And that's who you're going to spend your Christmas with. And the room erupts in a chant where people start saying, vote, vote, vote, vote, vote. And literally it's like a locker room and they leave the conference room chanting, vote and go up there and vote for whatever's in front of them because they want to go home and be with their families. That's the play call they're running this year. The CR that they just passed today goes into until December 20th. Okay. Now we're supposed to go on holiday break like a week before that. They're going to have some real leverage if we get to December 20th and people are missing their family Christmas parties and stuff. So that's one thing they're doing. It's messed up and I don't care whether you're Republican, Democrat, independent or libertarian. You should know that that's messed up. Here's the other thing that they did today. A funding bill, they put them all together. There should be 12 separate appropriations bills. But they've come to favor this strategy where they put it all together. So if it doesn't pass, it would be unforgivable for you not to vote to fund the whole government, right? So there's tremendous pressure because you're not incrementally voting for this or that. You're voting for all of government in one vote. They've realized they can attach some nasty stuff to that. A year or two ago, what they attached was called fixed nicks. It was an expansion of the broken background check system without fixing the, you know, for gun purchases, federal background check system. They threw that into an omnibus or a CR. Well, this, today, they threw in an extension of the Patriot Act into the omnibus. So, again, whether your republican democrat big l libertarian mall small l libertarian you should understand this is a horrible way to do legislation but they're using what they're doing is they're giving all the democrats who when republicans who were in the majority the democrats opposed for them up most of them opposed the patriot act but now today they gave them all cover date that they stuck the patriot act in the continuing resolution and so the democrats We could go home and say well head to vote for it now. Here's another thing they do Brian another messed up process And I know we're not talking about ideology here which may have set them the libertarians that listen to show But if they've got blood coursing through their veins if they can fog a mirror this should upset them Regardless of what their ideology is When Pelosi was Speaker before I got here, she famously said he got a vote for this Obamacare to see what's in it. Okay, I'm paraphrasing a little bit, but not as badly as Adam Schiff reading a transcript of the President. She said, you know, vote for it to see what's in it. Well, when Republicans took over, thanks to the Tea Party in 2010, they demanded we don't ever want to be in that position again, give us three days to read a bill. So the Republicans adopted a house rule that says everybody will have three days to read the bill. Well, nobody defined what a day is. Now, you and I think a day has 24 hours, but what they decided was that if you introduce the bill at 1150 PM on a Tuesday, then Tuesday counts as one day because the bill touched it by 10 minutes. You would have Wednesday to look at the bill. But guess what? The reporters can't get that printed in your hometown newspaper before Thursday morning, which is when you're going to vote on it.",
